  "body": "## What changed\n\nPinning a ribbon cell wrote the `RibbonPins` singleton straight from the pane (`panes.rs` `toggle_pin` → `ribbon::pinned_set`). Pins are saved in the project file, so this was a document change the history never saw: it couldn't be undone and couldn't mark the document unsaved, against AGENTS.md's \"Everything Is a Command\".\n\n- **New command `SetRibbonPins`** (`crates/app/src/commands/ribbon_pins.rs`, modelled on `SetTheme`). It records the previous and next pin lists, cleans the new list the way `pinned_set` does (duplicates and out-of-range indices dropped), and refuses a no-op, so nothing empty lands on the undo stack.\n- **`toggle_pin`** runs the command through `state.history` instead of writing the world directly. The fifth-pin refusal (`MAX_PINS`) still happens before any command is built, so it pushes nothing.\n- **Comments:** the M6.2 \"pins are layout, not a command\" comments in `ribbon.rs`, `schema.rs`, `panes.rs` and the `ribbon` suite header now describe the new behaviour.\n\n**The \"goes dirty\" half:** PR #141 (#107, unmerged) tracks unsaved changes from the history depth (`History::is_dirty`). Once it lands, a pin marks the document unsaved with no further change. This PR is based on `main`, not stacked on #141, so it can merge on its own. The tests pin the history half now (`can_undo` after a pin). After #141 merges, an `is_dirty()` assertion can go next to them; I'm happy to add it in a follow-up.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test ribbon`: 11 passed (one new).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 237 passed (two new, one updated). The one failure is `headless_run_succeeds`, which also fails on `main` here (macOS: \"No suitable graphics adapter found … metal had no fallback adapters\", an environment issue).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`: the remaining failures exist without this change too:\n  - the three headless-GPU tests (`headless_run_succeeds`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`): no fallback adapter on this Mac\n  - the two cross-drill tests in #151\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `ribbon::a_pin_is_a_command_undo_restores_the_previous_pins` (app): apply, undo, redo, the cleaned list, and the no-op refusal.\n- `egui_app::pin_tests::pinning_a_ribbon_cell_is_undoable` (ui): the real `toggle_pin` gesture walked by Undo/Redo.\n- `egui_app::pin_tests::a_refused_fifth_pin_pushes_nothing` (ui).\n- Updated: `egui_app::tests::right_click_pins_and_undo_replays_only_the_cuts` is renamed to `right_click_pins_and_undo_takes_the_pin_back`. It asserted the old behaviour (undo skips the pin); it now checks that the first undo takes the pin back, the second takes the cut back, and redo restores both.\n\nChangelog: Pinning or unpinning a ribbon cell can now be undone (Ctrl+Z) and counts as a document change\n\nFixes #143\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
